      "side": 1,
      "message": "They exist to ensure a smooth transition back to the IDLE state, even if APIs are called by higher-priority tasks (console or TPM) during one of the deferred function calls.  For example:\n\n1) ccdunlock requests short sequence\n2) physical_detect_done() is about to call the callback\n3) some higher-priority task does physical_detect_abort()\n4) some higher-priority task does ccdopen, which requests a long sequence\n5) physical_detect_done() calls the callback\n\nIf aborting went directly back to IDLE, then after step 3 the state machine would be idle.  So in step 4 the ccdopen request would succeed, and would set the callback to ccdopen_done.  But then when we return to step 5 it would call ccdopen_done(), not ccdunlock_done().\n\nI don\u0027t want to hold the mutex during the entire of physical_detect_done() because then physical_detect_start() and physical_detect_abort() will block until the callback finishes, instead of being able to error out with EC_ERROR_BUSY.\n\nThere are a couple of other race conditions like this.",
      "parentUuid": "4a456afd_c006da79",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 40,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 40,
        "endChar": 20
      },
